```js
const canvas = document.getElementById('game');
const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
const W = canvas.width, H = canvas.height;

// Audio
let audioCtx = null;
function beep(freq, dur=0.08, type='square', vol=0.15){
  try{
    if(!audioCtx) audioCtx = new (window.AudioContext||window.webkitAudioContext)();
    const o = audioCtx.createOscillator();
    const g = audioCtx.createGain();
    o.type = type; o.frequency.value = freq;
    g.gain.setValueAtTime(vol, audioCtx.currentTime);
    g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.001, audioCtx.currentTime+dur);
    o.connect(g); g.connect(audioCtx.destination);
    o.start(); o.stop(audioCtx.currentTime+dur);
  }catch(e){}
}

const state = {
  mode: 'ready', // ready, playing, levelclear, gameover, win
  score: 0, lives: 3, level: 1, maxLevel: 5,
  combo: 0,
};

const paddle = { x: W/2, w: 110, h: 12, y: H-30, speed: 620, wideTimer: 0 };

let balls = [];
let blocks = [];
let powerups = [];
let particles = [];

function newBall(stuck=true){
  return { x: paddle.x, y: paddle.y-9, vx:0, vy:0, r:8, stuck };
}

const LEVELS = [...]; // patterns as strings

function buildLevel(n){
  blocks = [];
  const pattern = LEVELS[(n-1)%LEVELS.length];
  const cols = pattern[0].length;
  const bw = 58, bh = 22, gap = 6;
  const totalW = cols*(bw+gap)-gap;
  const ox = (W-totalW)/2, oy = 60;
  for(let r=0;r<pattern.length;r++){
    for(let c=0;c<cols;c++){
      const ch = pattern[r][c];
      if(ch==='.') continue;
      const hp = ch==='3'?3: ch==='2'?2:1;
      blocks.push({x: ox+c*(bw+gap), y: oy+r*(bh+gap), w:bw, h:bh, hp, maxhp:hp});
    }
  }
}
```

Colors by hp: hp3 red (#e74c3c), hp2 orange/yellow (#f39c12), hp1 teal/blue (#3498db). Damage darkens the color.

Ball physics: speed magnitude constant per level, e.g. 340 + level*30.

Paddle collision: if ball moving down and intersects paddle rect: reflect vy, set vx based on offset:
```
const rel = (ball.x - paddle.x)/(paddle.w/2); // -1..1
const angle = rel * (Math.PI/3); // max 60deg
const sp = Math.hypot(ball.vx, ball.vy);
ball.vx = sp*Math.sin(angle);
ball.vy = -sp*Math.cos(angle);
```

Block collision: iterate blocks, circle-rect test:
```
function circleRectHit(b, r){
  const cx = Math.max(r.x, Math.min(b.x, r.x+r.w));
  const cy = Math.max(r.y, Math.min(b.y, r.y+r.h));
  const dx = b.x-cx, dy = b.y-cy;
  return dx*dx+dy*dy <= b.r*b.r;
}
```
Then determine bounce axis: compute overlap on each axis:
```
const overlapX = Math.min(b.x + b.r - r.x, r.x + r.w - (b.x - b.r));
```
Hmm, simpler: compare penetration on x vs y:
```
const px = (b.x - (r.x + r.w/2)) * r.w; // sign-based
```
Standard approach:
```
const dx = b.x - (r.x + r.w/2);
const dy = b.y - (r.y + r.h/2);
const crossX = (r.w/2 + b.r) - Math.abs(dx); // overlap if >0
const crossY = (r.h/2 + b.r) - Math.abs(dy);
if (crossX < crossY) ball.vx = dx>0? |vx| : -|vx|;
else ball.vy = dy>0? |vy| : -|vy|;
```
This is the classic method and works well enough.

Power-ups: on block destroy, 12% chance to drop. Types: 'E' expand, 'M' multiball, 'L' life. Fall at 140 px/s, caught by paddle.

Particles on block destroy: simple colored squares.

Level clear: all blocks destroyed → mode 'levelclear', show message, advance on click / Space.

Life loss: all balls fall → lives--, if 0 then gameover, else reset ball stuck to paddle.

Rendering: dark background, HUD at top (score, level, lives). Draw overlay text per mode.

